ll-America tailback Ahmad Hardy is set to make his season debut for the Tigers this weekend at Arkansas, sources told ESPN.","published":"2026-10-30T02:30:33.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50321651/sources-missouri-rb-hardy-make-season-debut-vs-arkansas","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Pete Thamel","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Missouri RB Ahmad Hardy to practice for first time since getting shot","description":"Missouri consensus All-America RB Ahmad Hardy, who was shot at a concert in May and has yet to play this season, will return to practice this week.","published":"2026-10-25T21:41:45.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50280668/mizzou-rb-hardy-practice-1st-getting-shot","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Alex Scarborough","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Missouri Tigers will be without Ahmad Hardy in season opener","description":"Missouri running back Ahmad Hardy will not be available in the season opener, and when asked about a timetable for a return Saturday, Tigers coach Eli Drinkwitz said that \"it's up to his body and his response, and I know he's doing everything he can.\"","published":"2026-08-23T01:59:51.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/49695877/missouri-rb-hardy-ready-season-opener-sources-said","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Pete Thamel","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Missouri's Ahmad Hardy healed from gunshot wound; status still TBD","description":"Missouri RB Ahmad Hardy has been cleared and is expected to make a full recovery from a gunshot wound to the leg, but his timetable for a return remains unclear.","published":"2026-07-20T16:51:16.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/49410596/missouri-ahmad-hardy-healed-gunshot-wound-return-date-unclear","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Andrea Adelson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Missouri's Ahmad Hardy starts road to rehab, thanks supporters","description":"Ahmad Hardy is back in Missouri just over a week after the All-America running back was shot in his home state of Mississippi. Missouri's football program released a 14-second video Wednesday in which Hardy said he was \"starting the road to my rehab.\"","published":"2026-05-20T19:50:16.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/48828415/missouri-ahmad-hardy-starts-road-rehab-thanks-supporters","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Suspect arrested in shooting of Missouri RB Ahmad Hardy","description":"A 20-year-old man wanted in connection to the shooting of Missouri football star Ahmad Hardy at an outdoor concert in Mississippi has been arrested.","published":"2026-05-16T13:30:30.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/48780471/suspect-arrested-shooting-missouri-rb-ahmad-hardy","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Missouri's Ahmad Hardy out of hospital after shooting","description":"Missouri running back Ahmad Hardy is out of the hospital after being shot early Sunday. Coach Eli Drinkwitz said he's unsure if Hardy would be able to play in 2026.","published":"2026-05-13T16:34:33.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/48752569/sources-mizzou-ahmad-hardy-hospital-shooting","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Missouri running back Ahmad Hardy shot, in stable condition","description":"Missouri running back Ahmad Hardy, a first-team All-SEC selection last season, was shot at a concert in Mississippi early Sunday and is in stable condition following surgery.","published":"2026-05-11T18:23:09.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/48741126/missouri-running-back-ahmad-hardy-shot-stable-condition","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5197065/ahmad-hardy","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ahmad_Hardy"},"pick":{"pick":61,"round":2,"team":"DEN","provisional":true},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Ahmad Hardy","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ahmad_Hardy","description":"American football player (born 2005)","touched":"2026-11-22T04:17:44Z","intro":"Ahmad Hardy (born December 19, 2005) is an American college football running back for the Missouri Tigers. He previously played for the Louisiana–Monroe Warhawks.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life and high school career","text":"Hardy was born in Brookhaven, Mississippi and grew up in the small community of Oma, Mississippi. He attended Lawrence County High School in Monticello, Mississippi. As a senior, he rushed for 2,442 yards and 27 touchdowns, before committing to play college football at the University of Louisiana at Monroe."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"LOUISIANA–MONROE\nHardy earned immediate playing time as a true freshman. In his collegiate debut against Jackson State, Hardy rushed for 103 yards and a touchdown in a 30–14 win. Against Troy, he rushed for 94 yards and the game's only touchdown, leading the Warhawks to a 13–9 victory. Against Southern Miss, he totaled 174 all-purpose yards, while rushing for two touchdowns in a 38–21 win. Hardy finished his freshman season rushing for 1,351 yards and 13 touchdowns, before announcing his intentions to enter the transfer portal. Hardy was named the Sun Belt Freshman of the Year and also received first-team all-conference honors at the end of the season.\n\nMISSOURI\nOn December 18, 2024, Hardy announced that he would be transferring to the University of Missouri to play for the Missouri Tigers. On September 13, 2025, Hardy rushed for 250 yards on 22 carries and scored three touchdowns against the Louisiana Ragin' Cajuns. This total ranks as the seventh-highest single-game rushing performance in Missouri history and is tied for the 22nd-most rushing yards in a game by a Southeastern Conference player. On November 15, 2025, in Missouri's 49–27 victory over Mississippi State, Hardy rushed for 300 yards and 3 touchdowns on 25 carries, becoming only the second Missouri player to have 300 rushing yards in a game, the other being Devin West (319 yards on 33 carries) in 1998 against Kansas. Hardy's rushing total was also the third-highest in a game in SEC history, behind Darren McFadden of Arkansas in 2007 and Tre Mason of Auburn in 2013 (whose 304-yard performance was against Missouri). Hardy is the second Missouri player to rush for 250 or more yards in two separate games in a season, after West did this twice in 1998."}]}}